{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>Until the time that …</b> — meaning, when time passes over the event, the anger by itself cools from its boiling. And she said further <b>until your brother's anger turns away</b> — meaning: for this alone will not suffice, but only until your brother's anger turns away <b>from you</b> — meaning, that even when they mention you before him, his anger will not flare. And this is what she says <b>from you</b> — that is a sign that he has forgotten the matter, etc." "<b>and I will send</b> etc. — meaning, I will send for you when this comes to pass, but you shall not come under any circumstances."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:06.267061644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}